WEBVTT

00:02:28.190 --> 00:02:29.280
Can you hear me?

00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:44.430
Hey, can you hear me?

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:55.230
Can you...

00:03:00.590 --> 00:03:01.950
August...

00:03:03.690 --> 00:03:04.850
4th.

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:07.500
Hey, you.

00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:12.000
Hey, what's wrong?

00:03:12.470 --> 00:03:15.190
I heard a scream. Are you all right?

00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:21.240
Someone'll be coming for you soon.

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:24.560
Um...

00:03:25.960 --> 00:03:26.980
Come on now.

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:29.260
Be patient and wait.

00:03:29.950 --> 00:03:32.370
<i>Who is she?</i>

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:40.490
I wonder who's coming for you.

00:03:44.420 --> 00:03:47.100
Are you all right?

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:49.910
You suddenly collapsed, so I was worried.

00:03:57.700 --> 00:04:00.660
What's all this about you collapsing?

00:04:04.990 --> 00:04:05.850
<i>Who is he?</i>

00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:09.850
Hey,

00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:12.240
are you really all right?

00:04:13.550 --> 00:04:17.610
<i>I don't know this person.</i>

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:21.690
I'll walk you home, so hurry up and get ready.

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:26.080
At least answer me.

00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:29.200
Yes.

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:32.080
I heard you collapsed.

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:35.820
Toma, why are you here, too?

00:04:35.820 --> 00:04:38.000
Because Sawa contacted me.

00:04:39.260 --> 00:04:41.720
Are you all right? You didn't hit anything, did you?

00:04:43.140 --> 00:04:45.040
What are you spacing out for?

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:48.260
Are you even listening?

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:54.180
Shin, don't pressure her like that.

00:04:54.180 --> 00:04:57.340
She just woke up. What do you expect?

00:04:57.340 --> 00:04:59.430
I know you're worried.

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:04.780
Now, before we go home, should we stop by the hospital?

00:05:07.270 --> 00:05:09.340
We probably should.

00:05:09.340 --> 00:05:10.130
Okay.

00:05:10.130 --> 00:05:11.600
You can't!

00:05:12.490 --> 00:05:16.120
You can't go to the hospital. That would only complicate things!

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:20.360
Just tell them you're sleepy and fake it.

00:05:21.830 --> 00:05:22.420
Okay.

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:24.060
So we're going to the hospital.

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:26.330
No.

00:05:27.790 --> 00:05:28.560
Which is it?

00:05:29.030 --> 00:05:32.160
I think I'm just tired.

00:05:32.960 --> 00:05:33.810
I'll go home.

00:05:34.590 --> 00:05:38.070
What have you been doing that would make you tired enough to pass out?

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:38.230
You're always—

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:38.770
Now, now.

00:05:39.640 --> 00:05:42.240
If that's all it is, we'll take you home.

00:05:46.670 --> 00:05:48.810
We're not walking too fast, are we?

00:05:49.750 --> 00:05:50.750
No.

00:05:55.390 --> 00:05:56.710
It's getting cold.

00:05:56.710 --> 00:06:00.660
It's only August, so what's up with this weather?

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:02.290
Just when you think the rainy season's over,

00:06:02.290 --> 00:06:04.880
summer's passed you by, and it's already fall.

00:06:06.180 --> 00:06:08.560
By the way, Shin, what happened to prep school?

00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:10.160
I left early.

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:13.210
Is that okay?

00:06:13.210 --> 00:06:15.630
I'm doing what needs to be done. I don't need your shit.

00:06:15.630 --> 00:06:18.370
Aren't you just the cutest little brother ever?

00:06:18.370 --> 00:06:21.300
Screw you. You're not my older brother.

00:06:21.300 --> 00:06:25.230
This part of him hasn't changed since he was a kid, right?

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:27.700
Weren't you listening?

00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:31.850
<i>I can't keep up with the conversation.</i>

00:06:31.850 --> 00:06:34.460
<i>I'm acquainted with these people, but I can't remember.</i>

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:36.170
Hey, I think she...

00:06:36.170 --> 00:06:38.090
Lay off already. Stop acting like an old woman.

00:06:38.090 --> 00:06:38.870
<i>Nothing.</i>

00:06:38.870 --> 00:06:39.460
Old woman?

00:06:39.900 --> 00:06:42.040
You get in everyone's business like an old woman.

00:06:42.040 --> 00:06:43.840
I'm just worried about her.

00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:45.060
<i>There's nothing.
Besides, you...</i>

00:06:45.060 --> 00:06:46.650
It's none of your business.

00:06:47.730 --> 00:06:48.110
Don't blame me if you fail your exams in spring.

00:06:48.110 --> 00:06:50.260
<i>It's not just them.</i>

00:06:50.260 --> 00:06:51.240
<i>Who exactly am I?</i>

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:52.790
That's not gonna happen.

00:06:54.450 --> 00:06:55.120
Hey.

00:06:58.030 --> 00:06:59.400
Where are you going?

00:07:01.210 --> 00:07:03.070
This is your house, right?

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:04.550
Here?

00:07:04.550 --> 00:07:06.990
You are <i>really</i> out of it.

00:07:06.990 --> 00:07:08.860
Will you be all right by yourself?

00:07:10.140 --> 00:07:12.850
Should we stick around for a little longer?

00:07:12.850 --> 00:07:15.250
You don't have to baby her that much.

00:07:15.250 --> 00:07:17.080
You're too harsh.

00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:19.080
Um...

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:21.370
I'm going to bed as soon as I get in.

00:07:22.140 --> 00:07:24.970
Thank you both for walking me home.

00:07:26.620 --> 00:07:28.240
Are you really all right?

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:29.090
Yes.

00:07:29.570 --> 00:07:30.610
But...

00:07:30.610 --> 00:07:32.160
Hey. Let's go.

00:07:32.910 --> 00:07:34.640
Don't drag me.

00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:37.060
If anything comes up, don't hesitate to call.

00:07:38.690 --> 00:07:39.960
Get some sleep.

00:07:46.920 --> 00:07:48.030
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:07:48.670 --> 00:07:50.020
You don't know?

00:07:50.960 --> 00:07:52.160
I thought so.

00:07:55.500 --> 00:08:00.500
You lost all your memories from before August 1st.

00:08:01.350 --> 00:08:02.320
I did?

00:08:03.230 --> 00:08:05.390
I've been with you for four days,

00:08:05.390 --> 00:08:07.940
but you don't know who I am anymore, do you?

00:08:07.940 --> 00:08:09.490
I'm sorry.

00:08:09.490 --> 00:08:11.510
You seem to be confused about a lot of things,

00:08:11.510 --> 00:08:13.180
so I'll explain everything from the start.

00:08:13.630 --> 00:08:16.010
First, let's start with the introductions.

00:08:16.010 --> 00:08:17.810
My name is Orion.

00:08:17.810 --> 00:08:22.880
I'm a spirit from a world separate from this one.

00:08:22.880 --> 00:08:23.940
A spirit?

00:08:23.940 --> 00:08:24.780
That's right.

00:08:24.780 --> 00:08:28.830
Just so you know, only you can see me,

00:08:28.830 --> 00:08:31.150
and my voice can't be heard by others either.

00:08:33.870 --> 00:08:37.460
What? You're looking at me like I'm an insect.

00:08:37.460 --> 00:08:39.890
I don't think you're an insect or anything.

00:08:39.890 --> 00:08:43.580
You had the same reaction when you first met me.

00:08:44.670 --> 00:08:45.590
That's all right, though.

00:08:45.880 --> 00:08:47.000
Well,

00:08:47.740 --> 00:08:49.090
actually...

00:08:49.980 --> 00:08:51.410
Um...

00:08:51.410 --> 00:08:55.600
Well, actually, it's my fault.

00:08:55.600 --> 00:08:59.170
I mean, why you lost your memories.

00:08:59.170 --> 00:09:01.690
To my surprise, when I came to this world,

00:09:01.690 --> 00:09:05.430
I bumped into your spirit, you know?

00:09:05.430 --> 00:09:07.800
It was a real problem for me, too.

00:09:10.740 --> 00:09:12.270
I'm really sorry!

00:09:13.390 --> 00:09:16.230
What do you mean by that?

00:09:16.230 --> 00:09:19.400
In place of the memories that you lost...

00:09:20.190 --> 00:09:23.870
I'm basically trapped in your soul.

00:09:24.140 --> 00:09:25.960
Wait a second.

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:28.890
I don't understand what you're saying.

00:09:28.890 --> 00:09:33.970
Wait. Why can't I go to the hospital?

00:09:33.970 --> 00:09:36.620
Because going to the hospital won't do you any good.

00:09:37.600 --> 00:09:43.010
Your memory loss isn't caused by any trouble with your mind or body.

00:09:43.010 --> 00:09:47.420
You have to get it back by interacting with others.

00:09:47.420 --> 00:09:52.180
If you're hospitalized instead and end up all alone,

00:09:52.180 --> 00:09:56.870
you won't be able to talk to people and reestablish the connections you once had with them.

00:09:56.870 --> 00:09:59.810
If that isolation from stimuli continues,

00:09:59.810 --> 00:10:01.850
you'll even forget things like how to drink water,

00:10:01.850 --> 00:10:05.210
or how to breathe, and you'll break—

00:10:06.910 --> 00:10:08.770
So to make sure that doesn't happen,

00:10:08.770 --> 00:10:12.750
you need to avoid mentioning you have amnesia and act carefully—

00:10:12.750 --> 00:10:13.800
But...

00:10:14.440 --> 00:10:18.080
I still don't understand anything.

00:10:18.080 --> 00:10:21.270
I can't even remember who I am.

00:10:21.270 --> 00:10:22.240
Sorry.

00:10:23.280 --> 00:10:25.740
Is she really all right?

00:10:27.090 --> 00:10:29.840
I wonder if she can make the trip in her current condition.

00:10:30.670 --> 00:10:33.800
Let's just keep an eye on things for now.

00:10:34.670 --> 00:10:36.400
I'm counting on you to cover for her at work.

00:10:36.400 --> 00:10:39.200
Of course, that's what I was planning on doing.

00:10:39.460 --> 00:10:43.700
I wonder if Shin and Toma, the two who walked you home, work at the same place you do.

00:10:44.320 --> 00:10:48.740
On the way home, they were talking like you were all old friends.

00:10:48.740 --> 00:10:49.890
You're right.

00:10:51.220 --> 00:10:54.620
But even when they brought up old stories, you didn't respond,

00:10:54.620 --> 00:10:56.920
so I wonder if they suspected something.

00:10:56.920 --> 00:10:57.720
Yeah.

00:10:58.830 --> 00:11:02.190
This is all the data I have.

00:11:02.190 --> 00:11:05.330
For some reason, all the data before now was erased.

00:11:05.330 --> 00:11:10.540
But it was good that your work contacts were able to be retrieved.

00:11:10.540 --> 00:11:11.720
Yeah.

00:11:11.720 --> 00:11:13.720
You might be right, but...

00:11:15.990 --> 00:11:17.060
Hey, hey.

00:11:17.060 --> 00:11:21.050
Did anything happen today that might give you a clue to your lost memories?

00:11:22.990 --> 00:11:26.140
<i>Why can't I think of anything?</i>

00:11:26.140 --> 00:11:29.420
<i>Can I really get my memories back?</i>

00:11:29.420 --> 00:11:30.560
Are you all right?

00:11:31.470 --> 00:11:33.120
<i>Maybe it's impossible.</i>

00:11:33.120 --> 00:11:34.440
Hey, you!

00:11:36.520 --> 00:11:38.330
Can you hear me?

00:11:39.420 --> 00:11:40.590
I'm sorry.

00:11:41.390 --> 00:11:44.820
It's been a rough day, so you must be tired.

00:11:44.820 --> 00:11:46.660
You should get some sleep.

00:11:47.810 --> 00:11:48.850
Yeah.

00:11:50.660 --> 00:11:56.400
I... I'm gonna do my best for you, so...

00:11:58.250 --> 00:12:03.490
Good night.

00:12:23.440 --> 00:12:25.830
Who am I?

00:12:45.450 --> 00:12:48.810
Good morning.

00:12:48.810 --> 00:12:52.080
Do you still remember what happened yesterday?

00:12:52.080 --> 00:12:54.030
Yes, I do.

00:12:54.030 --> 00:12:58.080
That's great! So you were just a little confused.

00:12:59.060 --> 00:13:02.470
It seems like your memories were all mixed up recently,

00:13:02.470 --> 00:13:04.270
but maybe you've finally calmed down.

00:13:04.270 --> 00:13:05.400
Thank goodness!

00:13:05.950 --> 00:13:09.450
If anything's bothering you, you can talk to me.

00:13:09.800 --> 00:13:12.900
From your perspective, you're surrounded by strangers,

00:13:12.900 --> 00:13:17.090
and it must be scary not knowing who you can trust.

00:13:17.090 --> 00:13:17.960
But...

00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:23.170
But in order to get your memories back,

00:13:23.170 --> 00:13:25.090
I'll support you any way I can!

00:13:25.970 --> 00:13:28.720
So let's do our best together!

00:13:30.700 --> 00:13:31.410
Yeah.

00:13:33.150 --> 00:13:35.090
Thank you, Orion.

00:13:36.970 --> 00:13:39.520
You called me by my name for the first time!

00:13:41.330 --> 00:13:44.590
But this isn't the time for idle chitchat!

00:13:45.290 --> 00:13:47.870
If we don't hurry, you'll be late for work!

00:13:49.850 --> 00:13:52.320
I have to go now. Sorry.

00:13:53.040 --> 00:13:56.060
Ikki! I'm coming to your café again today!

00:13:56.060 --> 00:13:56.980
Thank you.

00:13:58.760 --> 00:13:59.500
Excuse me.

00:14:01.360 --> 00:14:04.550
Good morning, everyone.

00:14:05.260 --> 00:14:07.900
Let's put some energy into our work again today.

00:14:09.050 --> 00:14:15.490
Recently, there have been some customers who have been exceedingly rude to our female staff.

00:14:15.490 --> 00:14:18.990
If anyone like that comes again today,

00:14:18.990 --> 00:14:20.620
please inform me immediately.

00:14:21.150 --> 00:14:22.400
I understand.

00:14:22.400 --> 00:14:24.210
Worst case, I will murder them with my own hands.

00:14:24.210 --> 00:14:26.150
Wh-What did he just say?

00:14:26.500 --> 00:14:28.130
What's he gonna do with his hands?

00:14:28.130 --> 00:14:30.930
That's all for today's meeting.

00:14:30.930 --> 00:14:34.190
Please fulfill your professional duties again today.

00:14:34.190 --> 00:14:34.870
Yes, sir.

00:14:35.350 --> 00:14:37.750
He's a strange manager, isn't he?

00:14:38.880 --> 00:14:39.600
Hey.

00:14:40.730 --> 00:14:42.550
Are you well enough to work?

00:14:43.130 --> 00:14:43.850
Yes.

00:14:43.850 --> 00:14:44.590
Really?

00:14:45.380 --> 00:14:46.520
I'm glad.

00:14:48.570 --> 00:14:50.960
Thank you very much...

00:14:54.990 --> 00:14:56.120
Is something...

00:15:01.650 --> 00:15:02.840
It's time to open.

00:15:02.840 --> 00:15:05.050
Ikki, do you have a moment?

00:15:05.050 --> 00:15:05.760
Yes.

00:15:07.040 --> 00:15:08.540
Let's do our best today as well.

00:15:08.540 --> 00:15:09.260
Okay.

00:15:10.520 --> 00:15:12.830
So his name's Ikki.

00:15:12.830 --> 00:15:15.490
Good-looking guy, but kind of shady.

00:15:15.490 --> 00:15:16.350
He was looking at you oddly just now.

00:15:16.350 --> 00:15:17.820
What is it, sir?

00:15:17.820 --> 00:15:18.640
I'll be stepping out for a while.

00:15:18.640 --> 00:15:19.680
Do you think so?

00:15:19.680 --> 00:15:20.500
I understand.

00:15:23.640 --> 00:15:24.500
Welcome.

00:15:26.650 --> 00:15:28.380
No, that's not right!

00:15:28.940 --> 00:15:32.160
You have to say, "Welcome back, masters."

00:15:32.960 --> 00:15:35.640
The manager is looking over here. Hurry.

00:15:36.570 --> 00:15:39.160
Welcome back, masters.

00:15:48.260 --> 00:15:50.930
The maid's handmade parfait, please.

00:15:50.930 --> 00:15:53.950
I'll have a large mille-feuille and a Darjeeling tea.

00:15:53.950 --> 00:15:57.030
Certainly, masters.

00:15:57.400 --> 00:16:00.340
I'll take care of the tea and cake.

00:16:00.810 --> 00:16:01.570
Okay,

00:16:02.440 --> 00:16:03.860
I'll leave it to you.

00:16:06.070 --> 00:16:09.230
Isn't the parfait your responsibility?

00:16:09.230 --> 00:16:12.890
It is called the maid's handmade, after all.

00:16:13.960 --> 00:16:14.930
I'm sorry.

00:16:15.530 --> 00:16:19.140
<i>What should I do? I don't know how to make a parfait.</i>

00:16:19.140 --> 00:16:21.890
Oh, no! An order she can't handle already!

00:16:22.490 --> 00:16:23.850
Um...

00:16:25.370 --> 00:16:27.570
What are you looking for?

00:16:27.910 --> 00:16:30.320
Don't tell me you've forgotten how to make it.

00:16:30.320 --> 00:16:30.830
Crap, I think he's suspicious.

00:16:30.830 --> 00:16:32.170
Um, I...

00:16:32.170 --> 00:16:33.210
Crap, I think he's suspicious.

00:16:33.210 --> 00:16:34.830
Place the flakes into the glass.

00:16:34.830 --> 00:16:36.890
Then fresh cream on top.

00:16:36.890 --> 00:16:39.920
Then arrange the fruit and add the ice cream.

00:16:39.920 --> 00:16:42.990
And then chocolate on top.

00:16:43.650 --> 00:16:45.540
And it's done.

00:16:47.600 --> 00:16:49.340
<i>What was that?</i>

00:16:49.610 --> 00:16:51.300
Are you all right?

00:16:54.650 --> 00:16:55.840
I'm so sorry.

00:16:59.750 --> 00:17:01.000
Come with me.

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:01.900
This way.

00:17:06.890 --> 00:17:07.950
Does it hurt?

00:17:07.950 --> 00:17:11.480
But if you tape it tightly, the bleeding will stop.

00:17:11.480 --> 00:17:13.390
Loosen it after a little bit.

00:17:14.220 --> 00:17:14.940
All right.

00:17:18.880 --> 00:17:21.180
It doesn't work on you, does it?

00:17:22.270 --> 00:17:24.990
He was staring at you before, too.

00:17:27.330 --> 00:17:28.450
Hey, Ken.

00:17:28.450 --> 00:17:29.340
Good morning.

00:17:29.830 --> 00:17:31.310
Good morning.

00:17:32.110 --> 00:17:34.540
I should get back to work, if that's all right with you.

00:17:34.540 --> 00:17:35.320
Okay.

00:17:35.320 --> 00:17:36.880
Thank you.

00:17:37.870 --> 00:17:38.820
See you.

00:17:41.600 --> 00:17:44.790
Sorry to make you help me.

00:17:44.790 --> 00:17:48.340
Were you the one who induced the Pauli effect on those glasses?

00:17:48.340 --> 00:17:49.610
Pau-what?

00:17:49.980 --> 00:17:51.620
The Pauli effect.

00:17:51.620 --> 00:17:57.030
The theoretical physicist Wolfgang Pauli was clumsy and often broke equipment.

00:17:57.030 --> 00:18:02.210
Apparently, he would sometimes break tools just by touching or being near them.

00:18:02.210 --> 00:18:05.720
Because he broke things so often, his colleagues teased him,

00:18:05.720 --> 00:18:08.820
saying it was due to a mysterious power.

00:18:08.820 --> 00:18:11.150
That is the origin of the Pauli effect.

00:18:11.150 --> 00:18:14.150
Basically, you are clumsy like Pauli.

00:18:14.150 --> 00:18:14.920
That took forever!

00:18:15.250 --> 00:18:17.550
A little passive-aggressive, too.

00:18:17.550 --> 00:18:23.850
Furthermore, working with an injured finger can lead to a bacterial infection.

00:18:23.850 --> 00:18:25.850
Perhaps you should go home for today.

00:18:26.400 --> 00:18:28.580
That's...

00:18:29.150 --> 00:18:31.310
We'd like to keep looking, right?

00:18:31.310 --> 00:18:33.400
Make up a reason to stay.

00:18:35.820 --> 00:18:39.130
Um... Uh...

00:18:40.500 --> 00:18:47.370
It's really not that bad, so I'd like to stay...

00:18:47.370 --> 00:18:49.920
Oh, and I've had plenty of rest...

00:18:49.920 --> 00:18:52.490
I'm sorry about all this.

00:18:52.490 --> 00:18:55.200
I'd like to spend more time getting used to this, so...

00:18:55.200 --> 00:18:57.880
Um, I'm an inconvenience, aren't I?

00:18:57.880 --> 00:18:59.750
So I'll...

00:18:59.750 --> 00:19:00.680
Excuse me.

00:19:01.220 --> 00:19:05.420
Could you say what you're trying to say more logically?

00:19:06.150 --> 00:19:11.330
If I could, I'd rather not leave early.

00:19:14.140 --> 00:19:16.230
<i>Did I make him angry?</i>

00:19:17.950 --> 00:19:21.630
His face is so inexpressive. I have no idea what he's thinking.

00:19:21.630 --> 00:19:22.880
Um... You see, I...

00:19:22.880 --> 00:19:23.700
I understand.

00:19:24.260 --> 00:19:28.340
You want to get more used to your job, right?

00:19:28.340 --> 00:19:31.210
Then we'll back you up.

00:19:32.390 --> 00:19:35.180
I'll explain the situation to the manager.

00:19:35.180 --> 00:19:39.970
With that intuitive explanation of yours, I fear he won't understand.

00:19:39.970 --> 00:19:41.720
Please.

00:19:43.260 --> 00:19:48.470
Could he have been quiet because he was trying to understand what you were saying?

00:19:50.010 --> 00:19:50.980
I see.

00:19:51.960 --> 00:19:53.430
If that's the case...

00:19:53.430 --> 00:19:56.000
Thank you.

00:19:58.320 --> 00:20:00.940
Welcome back, milady.

00:20:13.040 --> 00:20:14.580
That was a close call, wasn't it?

00:20:14.880 --> 00:20:16.600
Sorry.

00:20:17.380 --> 00:20:18.380
Be careful.

00:20:19.610 --> 00:20:20.050
Right.

00:20:36.920 --> 00:20:39.820
Take care, master.

00:20:45.390 --> 00:20:47.140
You worked hard today.

00:20:47.140 --> 00:20:48.290
Thank you.

00:20:48.290 --> 00:20:52.160
You were doing pretty well by the end.

00:20:52.160 --> 00:20:53.330
You think so?

00:20:53.790 --> 00:20:55.820
Let's work hard tomorrow, too.

00:20:55.820 --> 00:20:56.610
Yeah.

00:21:01.490 --> 00:21:02.300
Is that...

00:21:02.670 --> 00:21:03.780
...me?

00:21:04.970 --> 00:21:06.430
You're an eyesore.

00:21:06.430 --> 00:21:07.910
A backstabber.

00:21:09.850 --> 00:21:10.600
You...

00:21:11.330 --> 00:21:13.140
broke your promise, didn't you?

00:23:26.860 --> 00:23:29.130
Do you know what "Meido no Hitsuji" means?

00:23:29.130 --> 00:23:33.550
"Meido" means underworld, the realm of Pluto, and "hitsuji" means sheep; hence, "Pluto's Sheep."

00:23:33.550 --> 00:23:36.960
Well, the maid's handmade parfait looked delicious, didn't it?

00:23:36.960 --> 00:23:40.340
I wish I could eat your handmade parfait.
